                <pb facs="0789" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363 Am 6/98: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-18T17:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                                1921—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 19—10:10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>118. My August 12th, 10 a.m. British Minister insisting on immediate convoking of
                    Congress to special sessions in order that it may reconsider its decision on
                    Royal Bank matter, which he demands shall be arbitrated.</p>
                <pb facs="0790" n="666" xml:id="pg666"/>
                <p>President Acosta states Costa Rica will propose Chief Justice Taft as arbitrator
                    of both British claims.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
